        "original_id": "e62ca0e8-726d-5bb3-8630-3928c7cfe644",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Clara Schumann, Johannes Brahms, Bernhard Cossmann\n- Organizations: Hoch Conservatory\n- Places: Frankfurt\n- Roles: faculty member, cello teacher\n- Topics: music education, public performance, 19th-century classical music\n\nFacts:\n- In 1878, Bernhard Cossmann helped found the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt.\n- In 1878, Bernhard Cossmann became a teacher of cello at the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt.\n- In the late 19th century, Clara Schumann served on the faculty of the Hoch Conservatory.\n- In the late 19th century, the Hoch Conservatory achieved international renown with distinguished teachers such as Clara Schumann on its faculty.\n- Clara Schumann was the first person to perform any work by Johannes Brahms in public.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
