        "original_id": "56bd405a-fd72-5f3a-b8a3-9f882267b97c",
        "text": "Page: Hoch Conservatory. Sentence: Many distinguished have taught there: in the late 19th century, with such teachers as Clara Schumann on the faculty, the Conservatory achieved international renown.\nPage: Clara Schumann. Sentence: She was the first to perform publicly any work by Brahms.\nPage: Bernhard Cossmann. Sentence: However, in 1878, Cossmann helped found the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt, where he occupied the post of teacher of cello.",
